--- a/packaging/CHANGELOG.rst
+++ b/packaging/CHANGELOG.rst
@@ -23,6 +23,10 @@
 
 Fixes:
 
+* Reject tags whose interpreter is not a valid identifier (e.g.
+  ``2.7.6-none-any``): ``parse_tag()`` raises ``InvalidTag`` and
+  ``parse_wheel_filename()`` raises ``InvalidWheelFilename`` for wheel names
+  such as ``playlyfe-0.1.1-2.7.6-none-any.whl``.
 * Make ``Requirement.__hash__`` consistent with ``__eq__`` for
   trailing-zero-equivalent specifiers (e.g. ``foo==1.0.0`` and
   ``foo==1.0.0.0``), so equal requirements hash equal and deduplicate in
--- a/packaging/docs/tags.rst
+++ b/packaging/docs/tags.rst
@@ -41,6 +41,12 @@
 
 .. autoclass:: Tag
    :members:
+
+Each interpreter in a tag (every member of a compressed, dot-separated
+interpreter set) must be a valid identifier in the sense of
+:meth:`str.isidentifier`. :func:`parse_tag` raises :exc:`InvalidTag` for tags
+such as ``2-none-any``, ``2.7.6-none-any``, ``py3.2-none-any`` and
+``py+3-none-any``. ABI and platform components are only rejected when empty.
 
 .. autofunction:: parse_tag
 
--- a/packaging/docs/utils.rst
+++ b/packaging/docs/utils.rst
@@ -8,3 +8,8 @@
 
 .. automodule:: packaging.utils
     :members:
+
+:func:`parse_wheel_filename` raises :exc:`InvalidWheelFilename` when the tag
+set of a wheel filename is rejected by :func:`packaging.tags.parse_tag`, for
+example ``playlyfe-0.1.1-2.7.6-none-any.whl``, whose interpreter tags ``2``,
+``7`` and ``6`` are not valid identifiers.
